# API Integration

## Data Loading — Inertia Props Only

All data comes from Rails controllers as Inertia props. Never fetch data client-side.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — data from props, real-time via cable
const { sessions, cableStream } = usePage().props;
useInertiaCableStream(cableStream, { only: ['sessions'] });

// ❌ BAD — client-side fetch duplicates server truth
const [data, setData] = useState(null);
useEffect(() => { fetch('/api/...').then(...) }, []);
```

## Mutations — apiFetch

Use `shared/lib/apiFetch` for POST/PATCH/DELETE. It auto-injects CSRF token, credentials, and Accept header.

```tsx
import { apiFetch } from 'shared/lib/apiFetch';

await apiFetch('/terminal_sessions', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ terminalSession: { ... } }),
});
```

Never read CSRF tokens manually — `apiFetch` handles it.
